\label{thm:seagulls}
Let $k \geqslant 1$ be an integer and let $G$ be a graph with $\alpha(G) = 2$ and $G \ncong W_5$. Then $G$ has $k$ vertex-disjoint seagulls if and only if:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $|V(G)| \geqslant 3k$,
    \item $\kappa(G) \geqslant k$,
    \item For each clique $C \subseteq V(G)$, if $D$ is the set of vertices in $V(G) \setminus C$ that have both a neighbour and a non-neighbour in $C$, then $|D| + |V(G) \setminus C| \geqslant 2k$, and
    \item $\mu(\overline{G}) \geqslant k$.
\end{enumerate}

